.TH PINLEAF 1 "October 2026" "Pinleaf" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pinleaf \- local desktop sticky notes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pinleaf
.SH DESCRIPTION
Pinleaf is a GTK 4 and libadwaita desktop application for sticky notes.
Notes are saved automatically in a local SQLite library.
Profiles and groups organize notes; open Shared notes remain visible alongside
the active group's notes.
.PP
Use the main panel to create, search, organize and reopen notes.
Closing the panel hides it; use the status indicator to show it again or quit.
.PP
The Backup & Restore window saves portable whole-library backups, with optional
password protection, to a local file or Google Drive.
Google Drive operations require an explicit connection and a configured desktop
OAuth client. Starting Pinleaf and editing notes do not require a network.
.PP
Restore validates the chosen file and previews its contents before asking to
replace the library. A local recovery copy preserves the current library first.
Passwords for protected backups cannot be recovered by Pinleaf.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for local application data. Defaults to
.IR ~/.local/share .
.TP
.B PINLEAF_GOOGLE_CLIENT_FILE
Optional maintainer/development override for the registered desktop OAuth
client JSON. User access tokens are stored in the system keyring, or only in
session memory when that mode is explicitly selected.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/pinleaf/pinleaf.sqlite3
Local note library. With the default data directory, this is
.IR ~/.local/share/pinleaf/pinleaf.sqlite3 .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/pinleaf/backups/
Private local recovery backups. Removing the application package does not
remove note data or these recovery copies.
.SH AUTHOR
Carlos R Moraes.
.SH HOMEPAGE
.UR https://robmoraes.github.io/pinleaf/
.UE
